earchers will have access to the data. All documents will be securely stored in a locked file cabinet located in the Integrated Science Center for three years. After that period they will be shredded. <\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Your identity and responses will be protected to the extent allowed by law. This means that they will be treated as confidential, unless you disclose information that is construed as threatening to yourself\/others, or as indicative of abuse of minors\/vulnerable adults.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">There are no foreseeable risks to you from participating in this research. We hope that the research will benefit research in our field by providing information about reading comprehension and mind wandering. We also hope that by participating in this study you learn something about what issues are of interest to psychologists, and how research studies are designed and conducted. There will be no costs to you, other than your time involved. <\/span><br>\n&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Your participation in this research is voluntary. You are free to refuse to take part. You are free to withdraw your consent and discontinue participation in this study at any time by simply not responding to the questions. If you are participating in this study in order to receive credit for a class, rest assured that you may refuse to answer any question(s) that might make you feel uncomfortable and still receive course credit.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">No feedback on individual scores will be provided. You will be provided with a debriefing form when you have completed the survey. You may request a copy of the overall results of the research by calling, Claire Clarke, Matthew Kindem, Kaytlynn Ziegler, &nbsp;at 612-720-4940, 218-766-6231, 218-234-6877 or e-mailing at cclarke@cord.edu, mkindem2@cord.edu, kziegle1@cord.edu. <\/span><br>\n&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">If you have any questions about your rights or treatment as a participant in this research project, please contact Concordia College\u2019s Institutional Review Board at (218) 299-3001, or send a letter to Concordia College, Institutional Review Board, Office of Academic Affairs, 901 8<\/span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">th<\/span><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"> St. S., Moorhead, MN 56562.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Thank you.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">PLEASE FEEL FREE TO PRINT AND KEEP THIS SHEET FOR YOUR FUTURE REFERENCE<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br><\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64); font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 22.1px; font-weight: 400; white-space: normal;\">Do you agree to participate in this study?<\/span><\/span><\/p>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_en9q7gEnCvYC6VL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID724","SecondaryAttribute":"Concordia College, Moorhead, MN INFORMED CONSENT STATEMENT PLEASE READ BEFORE COMPLETING THE SURV...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><span style=\"font-size:13.999999999999998pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Concordia College, Moorhead, MN<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:13.999999999999998pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">INFORMED CONSENT STATEMENT<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">PLEASE READ BEFORE COMPLETING THE SURVEY<\/span><br>\n&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Hello, our names are Claire Clarke, Matthew Kindem, and Kaytlynn Ziegler. We are student researchers researchers in the department of psychology at Concordia College, Moorhead, MN. We would like to invite you to take part in our research concerning mind wandering. The purpose of this study is to investigate the link between mind wandering and reading comprehension. <\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">If you agree to take part in our research, you will be asked to fill out a survey that includes different passages to read and questions about &nbsp;the presented texts. Responding to the surveys should take about 30 minutes of your time. <\/span><span style=\"font-size: 15.3333px; white-space: pre-wrap;\">As a token of appreciation for your time, we will offer you the opportunity to enter a drawing for a $15 gift card upon completion of the survey.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Your responses will be confidential. Your name will not be linked to your responses. We will not use your name or other identifying information in any reports of the research. Only the researchers will have access to the data. All documents will be securely stored in a locked file cabinet located in the Integrated Science Center for three years. After that period they will be shredded. <\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Your identity and responses will be protected to the extent allowed by law. This means that they will be treated as confidential, unless you disclose information that is construed as threatening to yourself\/others, or as indicative of abuse of minors\/vulnerable adults.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">There are no foreseeable risks to you from participating in this research. We hope that the research will benefit research in our field by providing information about reading comprehension and mind wandering. We also hope that by participating in this study you learn something about what issues are of interest to psychologists, and how research studies are designed and conducted. There will be no costs to you, other than your time involved. <\/span><br>\n&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Your participation in this research is voluntary. You are free to refuse to take part. You are free to withdraw your consent and discontinue participation in this study at any time by simply not responding to the questions. If you are participating in this study in order to receive credit for a class, rest assured that you may refuse to answer any question(s) that might make you feel uncomfortable and still receive course credit.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">No feedback on individual scores will be provided. You will be provided with a debriefing form when you have completed the survey. You may request a copy of the overall results of the research by calling, Claire Clarke, Matthew Kindem, Kaytlynn Ziegler, &nbsp;at 612-720-4940, 218-766-6231, 218-234-6877 or e-mailing at cclarke@cord.edu, mkindem2@cord.edu, kziegle1@cord.edu. <\/span><br>\n&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">If you have any questions about your rights or treatment as a participant in this research project, please contact Concordia College\u2019s Institutional Review Board at (218) 299-3001, or send a letter to Concordia College, Institutional Review Board, Office of Academic Affairs, 901 8<\/span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">th<\/span><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"> St. S., Moorhead, MN 56562.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Thank you.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">PLEASE FEEL FREE TO PRINT AND KEEP THIS SHEET FOR YOUR FUTURE REFERENCE<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br><\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64); font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 22.1px; font-weight: 400; white-space: normal;\">Do you agree to participate in this study?<\/span><\/span><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Concordia College, Moorhead, MN INFORMED CONSENT STATEMENT PLEASE READ BEFORE COMPLETING THE SURV...","Choices":{"3":{"Display":"Yes"},"4":{"Display":"No"}},"ChoiceOrder":["3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p><span style=\"font-size:13.999999999999998pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Concordia College, Moorhead, MN<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:13.999999999999998pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">INFORMED CONSENT STATEMENT<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">PLEASE READ BEFORE COMPLETING THE SURVEY<\/span><br>\n&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Hello, our names are Claire Clarke, Matthew Kindem, and Kaytlynn Ziegler. We are student researchers researchers in the department of psychology at Concordia College, Moorhead, MN. We would like to invite you to take part in our research concerning mind wandering. The purpose of this study is to investigate the link between mind wandering and reading comprehension. <\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">If you agree to take part in our research, you will be asked to fill out a survey that includes different passages to read and questions about &nbsp;the presented texts. Responding to the surveys should take about 30 minutes of your time. <\/span><span style=\"font-size: 15.3333px; white-space: pre-wrap;\">As a token of appreciation for your time, we will offer you the opportunity to enter a drawing for a $15 gift card upon completion of the survey.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Your responses will be confidential. Your name will not be linked to your responses. We will not use your name or other identifying information in any reports of the research. Only the researchers will have access to the data. All documents will be securely stored in a locked file cabinet located in the Integrated Science Center for three years. After that period they will be shredded. <\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Your identity and responses will be protected to the extent allowed by law. This means that they will be treated as confidential, unless you disclose information that is construed as threatening to yourself\/others, or as indicative of abuse of minors\/vulnerable adults.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">There are no foreseeable risks to you from participating in this research. We hope that the research will benefit research in our field by providing information about reading comprehension and mind wandering. We also hope that by participating in this study you learn something about what issues are of interest to psychologists, and how research studies are designed and conducted. There will be no costs to you, other than your time involved. <\/span><br>\n&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Your participation in this research is voluntary. You are free to refuse to take part. You are free to withdraw your consent and discontinue participation in this study at any time by simply not responding to the questions. If you are participating in this study in order to receive credit for a class, rest assured that you may refuse to answer any question(s) that might make you feel uncomfortable and still receive course credit.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">No feedback on individual scores will be provided. You will be provided with a debriefing form when you have completed the survey. You may request a copy of the overall results of the research by calling, Claire Clarke, Matthew Kindem, Kaytlynn Ziegler, &nbsp;at 612-720-4940, 218-766-6231, 218-234-6877 or e-mailing at cclarke@cord.edu, mkindem2@cord.edu, kziegle1@cord.edu. <\/span><br>\n&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">If you have any questions about your rights or treatment as a participant in this research project, please contact Concordia College\u2019s Institutional Review Board at (218) 299-3001, or send a letter to Concordia College, Institutional Review Board, Office of Academic Affairs, 901 8<\/span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">th<\/span><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"> St. S., Moorhead, MN 56562.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Thank you.<\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">PLEASE FEEL FREE TO PRINT AND KEEP THIS SHEET FOR YOUR FUTURE REFERENCE<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br><\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64); font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 22.1px; font-weight: 400; white-space: normal;\">Do you agree to participate in this study?<\/span><\/span><\/p>","DataExportTag":"Q724","QuestionID":"QID724"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_en9q7gEnCvYC6VL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID552","SecondaryAttribute":"Curiously enough, another important artist of about the same time was scorned even by many of his...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p>Curiously enough, another important artist of about the same\ntime was scorned even by many of his own contemporaries.<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q189","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Curiously enough, another important artist of about the same time was scorned even by many of his...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":1,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID552","QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p>Curiously enough, another important artist of about the same\ntime was scorned even by many of his own contemporaries.<\/p>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_en9q7gEnCvYC6VL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID585","SecondaryAttribute":"Curiously, about the same time, another important artist was scorned even by many of his contempo...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p>Curiously, about the same time, another important artist was\nscorned even by many of his contemporaries.<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q423","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Curiously, about the same time, another important artist was scorned even by many of his contempo...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":1,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID585","QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p>Curiously, about the same time, another important artist was\nscorned even by many of his contemporaries.<\/p>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_en9q7gEnCvYC6VL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID77","SecondaryAttribute":"Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog Flush, but he seldom could be lured fr...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p>Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog\nFlush, but he seldom could be lured from his home evenings.&nbsp;<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q38","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog Flush, but he seldom could be lured fr...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":9,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID77","QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p>Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog\nFlush, but he seldom could be lured from his home evenings.&nbsp;<\/p>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_en9q7gEnCvYC6VL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID164","SecondaryAttribute":"Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog Flush, but he seldom could be lured fr...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p>Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog\nFlush, but he seldom could be lured from his home evenings.<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q259","QuestionID":"QID164","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog Flush, but he seldom could be lured fr...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":1,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p>Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog\nFlush, but he seldom could be lured from his home evenings.<\/p>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_en9q7gEnCvYC6VL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID722","SecondaryAttribute":"Debriefing Form Thank you for agreeing to participate in our research project. We greatly appreci...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div>Debriefing Form<\/div>\n\n<div>\n<div>Thank you for agreeing to participate in our research project. We greatly appreciate you taking<\/div>\n\n<div>the time to contribute to our research. We hope the study went well.<br>\n&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>We wanted to take a moment to explain a few more details of our study. We are interested in the<\/div>\n\n<div>association between reading task levels and mind wandering. There is some debate in research as<\/div>\n\n<div>to what reading levels result in more mind wandering. Some research indicates that mind<\/div>\n\n<div>wandering can occur more easily in easier tasks due to more available mental resources, but<\/div>\n\n<div>other research indicates that mind wandering occurs more easily in difficult tasks due to the task<\/div>\n\n<div>being less accessible and thus not sustaining attention well.<br>\n&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>If you have any questions regarding the survey please contact Claire Clarke at cclarke@cord.edu,<\/div>\n\n<div>or 612-720-4940.<br>\n&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div><strong>We will be continuing to recruit participants for this experiment and would appreciate if<\/strong><\/div>\n\n<div><strong>you did not share any elements of this study with friends or peers.<\/strong><\/div>\n\n<div>It may alter results if participants knew in advanced that the study was specifically about reading difficulty and mind<\/div>\n\n<div>wandering. Being aware of this my change participant performance on the study.<\/div>\n\n<div>Thank you again for participating in our study!<br>\n&nbsp;<\/div>\n<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q2","QuestionID":"QID722","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Debriefing Form Thank you for agreeing to participate in our research project. We greatly appreci...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><strong>Debriefing Statement<\/strong><\/span><\/span><\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>Thank you for ...<\/div>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_en9q7gEnCvYC6VL","Element":"RS","PrimaryAttribute":"RS_1ZzOfAOORmtPH1z","SecondaryAttribute":"Default Response Set","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":null},{"SurveyID":"SV_en9q7gEnCvYC6VL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID621","SecondaryAttribute":"Differences among individual subjects cannot systematically confound the results if assignment to...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p>Differences among individual subjects cannot systematically\nconfound the results if assignment to conditions is truly random.<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q212","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Differences among individual subjects cannot systematically confound the results if assignment to...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":1,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID621","QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p>Differences among individual subjects cannot systematically\nconfound the results if assignment to conditions is truly random.<\/p>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_en9q7gEnCvYC6VL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID723","SecondaryAttribute":"Do you agree to participate in this study?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Do you agree to participate in this study?","DataExportTag":"Q458","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Do you agree to participate in this study?","Choices":{"5":{"Display":"Yes"},"6":{"Display":"No"}},"ChoiceOrder":["5","6"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":7,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID723","RecodeValues":{"5":"1","6":"2"},"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_en9q7gEnCvYC6VL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID725","SecondaryAttribute":"Do you agree to participate in this study?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Do you agree to participate in this study?","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Do you agree to participate in this study?","Choices":{"5":{"Display":"Yes"},"6":{"Display":"No"}},"ChoiceOrder":["5","6"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":7,"NextAnswerId":1,"RecodeValues":{"5":"1","6":"2"},"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Do you agree to participate in this study?","DataExportTag":"Q725","QuestionID":"QID725"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_en9q7gEnCvYC6VL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID83","SecondaryAttribute":"During the third year of their stay in Italy, a son, Robert Weidemann Browning, was born.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p>During the third year of their stay in Italy, a son, Robert\nWeidemann Browning, was born.<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q43","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"During the third year of their stay in Italy, a son, Robert Weidemann Browning, was born.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":1,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID83","QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p>During the third year o